    [5749] = {
        description = "Use a tradable Vial of the Sands to become a drake that can carry a party member. The buyer needs no profession.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Buying the finished vial is straightforward but costly; discovering and crafting it yourself is a long random profession route.\n\n1. For the direct route, search the Auction House for Vial of the Sands, buy the finished item and use it. You do not need Alchemy or Archaeology, and riding as another player's passenger does not teach your own mount.\n\n2. For the self-crafted route, learn Cataclysm Alchemy on the character doing Archaeology and raise it to 75 for crafting. Level Archaeology far enough for Tol'vir projects. The recipe can be discovered only by an eligible Alchemist opening Canopic Jars; another character cannot mail you its bound recipe.\n\n3. Obtain Tol'vir fragments from original Uldum dig sites, or at Archaeology 600 exchange Restored Artifacts for Tol'vir fragment crates at Brann Bronzebeard in the Seat of Knowledge (83.5,31.0 in the Vale). Solve Tol'vir projects until Canopic Jar is offered, solve it and open the jar. Repeat until Recipe: Vial of the Sands appears. A jar is not guaranteed to contain it.\n\n4. Gather 12 Truegold, 8 Flasks of the Winds, 8 Flasks of Titanic Strength and 8 Deepstone Oil. Buy these from the Auction House or make them with the appropriate Cataclysm recipes. A crafter who already knows the recipe can also turn your materials into a finished tradable vial.\n\n5. Buy 1 Pyrium-Laced Crystalline Vial and 8 Sands of Time from Yasmin at 26.6,7.2 in northwestern Uldum. In original Uldum they total 29,000 gold at base price. The assault-era Yasmin uses Uldum Accord reputation discounts, bringing that vendor portion to 23,200 gold at Exalted; select the correct phase with Zidormi near Ramkahen.\n\n6. Craft Vial of the Sands or receive the completed vial from your crafter, then use it. Summon Sandstone Drake from the journal. Invite your passenger to your party and let them interact with you after you transform.",
