    [5751] = {
        achievementId = 5751,
        name = "2500 Daily Quests Completed",
        category = "Quests",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "2500 Daily Quests Completed",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Thousands of daily hand-ins, limited by the daily quests you have unlocked.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Thousands of daily hand-ins, limited by the daily quests you have unlocked.\n\n1. Track the achievement and note its current counter. Use actual DAILY quests with repeatable daily hand-ins; do not assume every modern world quest, weekly quest or repeatable turn-in uses this counter. A Retail comment specifically reports Zereth Mortis dailies failing to count.\n\n2. Take your capital's portal to Tol Barad Peninsula. Accept the available faction-camp dailies, finish their marked kill/collection objectives and RETURN to turn them in. The Peninsula quests are PvE and do not require winning the island battle.\n\n3. When your faction controls the southern Tol Barad island, cross the bridge and add the three outdoor dailies and the open prison's three dailies from the central quest hub. Inspect the achievement counter after hand-ins; these can also advance Breaking Out of Tol Barad and Just Another Day in Tol Barad.\n\n4. For more daily options, finish the Mount Hyjal story and unlock Sanctuary of Malorne / Molten Front dailies, or use the cooking/fishing city dailies described by their individual guides. Complete only quests whose first hand-in visibly advances this counter.\n\n5. Return after daily resets and repeat until 2,500 DAILY completions are recorded. Do not use launch-era calculations based on the old 25-daily cap as a current completion schedule; your unlocked quests and actual credited hand-ins determine the pace.",
