    [5752] = {
        achievementId = 5752,
        name = "Justly Rewarded",
        category = "Quests",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Justly Rewarded",
        difficulty = "medium",
        difficultyReason = "Earn thirty thousand gold specifically from quest rewards.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Earn thirty thousand gold specifically from quest rewards.\n\n1. Track Justly Rewarded and record its quest-gold total. This is a cumulative QUEST REWARD counter, different from the looted-gold achievements and from the amount currently in your bags.\n\n2. Complete available story and side quests on an eligible character, then TURN THEM IN and choose their rewards. The Cataclysm zone-story guides supply a connected route through Hyjal, Deepholm, Uldum, Vashj'ir and Twilight Highlands; current higher-level campaign quests can also be used when their hand-ins advance your counter.\n\n3. Check progress after the first hand-in. Count the quest's actual gold reward, not the later vendor value of its armor or an Auction House sale. Do not assume that a gold-looking world-quest reward necessarily updates this older counter without observing credit.\n\n4. Continue unfinished questlines and eligible daily hand-ins until 30,000 gold from quest rewards is recorded. Picking a higher-value reward item to sell may help your finances, but it does not turn that sale into quest-reward gold.",
